infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title What stops it: framework vs your code
  desc CSRF checks verify where a request came from, never what it may do
  compares
    - label Framework defends provenance
      children
        - label SameSite=Lax cookies
          desc Cross-site POST arrives without the session cookie
        - label Origin vs Host on every action
          desc Rejects forged origins, even sibling subdomains
        - label Closed-over values encrypted
          desc Per-build key; arguments stay plaintext
    - label Only your code defends the app
      children
        - label verifySession
          desc Kills anonymous calls to a UI-less endpoint
        - label Rate limit, 20 writes / 10s
          desc Kills credential stuffing and denial-of-wallet
        - label zod-parse the unknown payload
          desc Kills mass assignment (role admin via spread)
        - label Row ownership check
          desc Kills IDOR, the authentic request CSRF never sees
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
